Apache AGE (Apache-2.0) itself is a PostgreSQL EXTENSION loaded into the
customer's Postgres server (`LOAD 'age'`), not a Python dependency — it never
enters uv.lock or the C4 Python license gate. The production pin is
PostgreSQL 17 + AGE 1.7.0 (see README §R2); live conformance tests run against
`apache/age:release_PG17_1.6.0` (the newest published PG17 Docker image) over
the openCypher subset common to 1.6.0/1.7.0.

